IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-first-schedule`

-- g1-tests-first-schedule.l4: tests of g1-first-schedule.l4.  Group G1.
-- Every expected value below is decided from the First Schedule as printed (inputs/law.wiki lines 466 to 561, checked on
-- the gazette pages 198 to 201), before any rule was run:
--   Part A row 1 lists items (1) to (12); rows 2 and 3 list item (1), 'all the installation works listed in this column
--   for grade 1'.  Part B row 1 lists items (1) to (14); row 2 lists item (1), 'all the maintenance works listed in this
--   column for grade 1'; row 3 lists item (1) the same, and items (2) and (3), which no other row lists.
-- So A.1(1) to A.1(12) and B.1(1) to B.1(14) are listed under grades 1, 2 and 3, and B.3(2) and B.3(3) under grade 3 only.

§ `Tests of the First Schedule`

§§ `Which licence kinds the Schedule lists each activity under (28 activities)`

#ASSERT `licence kinds that may do the activity` `A.1(1) checking the permitted refrigerant quantity` EQUALS (LIST `grade 1 licence`, `grade 2 licence`, `grade 3 licence`)
#ASSERT `licence kinds that may do the activity` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units` EQUALS (LIST `grade 1 licence`, `grade 2 licence`, `grade 3 licence`)
